      "summaries": {
        "en": "Gallery is an open-source Android application that demonstrates practical on-device machine learning and generative AI implementations, enabling users to experience models locally without cloud dependency. Its technical insight lies in showcasing optimized model deployment through TensorFlow Lite and MediaPipe, illustrating how complex AI can run efficiently on mobile hardware. Developers can explore the codebase to learn implementation patterns, adapt the showcased use cases for their own projects, or use it as a testing platform for evaluating on-device AI performance directly on Android devices.",
        "zh": "Gallery 是一个开源 Android 应用，专门展示在设备端运行的机器学习和生成式 AI 的实际用例，让用户无需依赖云端即可本地体验模型。它通过集成 TensorFlow Lite 和 MediaPipe 等框架，演示了如何将复杂 AI 模型优化部署到移动设备，体现了边缘计算的高效性。开发者可以研究其代码学习实现模式，借鉴展示的用例开发自己的应用，或将其作为测试平台，直接在 Android 设备上评估端侧 AI 模型的性能与用户体验。",
        "es": "Gallery is an open-source Android application that demonstrates practical on-device machine learning and generative AI implementations, enabling users to experience models locally without cloud dependency. Its technical insight lies in showcasing optimized model deployment through TensorFlow Lite and MediaPipe, illustrating how complex AI can run efficiently on mobile hardware. Developers can explore the codebase to learn implementation patterns, adapt the showcased use cases for their own projects, or use it as a testing platform for evaluating on-device AI performance directly on Android devices.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "gallery gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Gallery is an open-source Android application that demonstrates practical on-device machine learning and generative AI implementations, enabling users to experience models locally without cloud dependency. Its technical insight lies in showcasing optimized model deployment through TensorFlow Lite and MediaPipe, illustrating how complex AI can run efficiently on mobile hardware. Developers can explore the codebase to learn implementation patterns, adapt the showcased use cases for their own projects, or use it as a testing platform for evaluating on-device AI performance directly on Android devices.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/google-ai-edge/gallery for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
